sequenceDiagram
    participant KServe as KServe InferenceService logger
    participant MM as ModelMesh payload processor
    participant User as User / ODH Dashboard
    participant Route as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant KRP as kube-rbac-proxy sidecar
    participant Health as health_app<br/>8080/TCP HTTP (no auth)
    participant App as Main app<br/>127.0.0.1:8081 HTTP / 4443 HTTPS
    participant Sched as Prometheus scheduler<br/>(in-process, 30s)
    participant Store as Storage<br/>PVC HDF5 / MariaDB 3306 / PostgreSQL 5432
    participant Prom as Prometheus / UWM
    participant Mig as trustyai-migrate

    Note over KServe,Store: Flow 1 - KServe inference logging ingest
    KServe->>Health: POST / CloudEvent (gzip optional)<br/>8080/TCP HTTP, plaintext, no auth
    Health->>Store: Persist joined request/response rows<br/>DB protocol, TLS if CA mounted, DB user/password
    Health-->>KServe: 200 OK

    Note over MM,Store: Flow 2 - ModelMesh payload ingest and reconciliation
    MM->>Health: POST /consumer/kserve/v2 (request part)<br/>8080/TCP HTTP, no auth
    Health->>Store: Buffer partial payload
    MM->>Health: POST /consumer/kserve/v2 (response part)
    Health->>Store: Reconcile by inference id, write rows<br/>TLS if CA mounted, DB credentials

    Note over User,Prom: Flow 3 - Metric registration and Prometheus publishing
    User->>Route: POST /metrics/group/fairness/spd/request<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS, Bearer token
    Route->>KRP: Forward
    KRP->>KRP: TokenReview / SubjectAccessReview
    KRP->>App: Proxy to 127.0.0.1:8081<br/>HTTP, pod-local
    App-->>KRP: Request id
    KRP-->>User: Response
    loop every SERVICE_METRICS_SCHEDULE (30s)
        Sched->>Store: Read inference data
        Store-->>Sched: Rows
        Sched->>Sched: Compute metrics, update gauges
    end
    Prom->>App: GET /q/metrics<br/>4443/TCP HTTPS TLS (or proxy port), per ServiceMonitor
    App-->>Prom: trustyai_* gauges

    Note over Mig,Store: Flow 4 - Legacy data migration
    Mig->>Store: Read legacy PVC HDF5/CSV or MariaDB tables<br/>3306/TCP, TLS CERT_REQUIRED if CA mounted
    Mig->>Store: Write canonical schema, namespaced tables<br/>asyncmy/asyncpg 3306/5432, TLS + hostname check if CA mounted
